				173,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Deps/Tauri): Correct extension path resolution documentation\n\nUpdate inline comments within the `PluginsWorkspace` submodule of the Land/Dependency/Tauri dependency. The previous documentation mischaracterized the `resolve_extension_path` logic regarding missing root indicators in Unix paths, failing to acknowledge that the implementation correctly preserves the full home directory structure.\n\nAlign the examples to demonstrate that emitted URLs maintain the complete path (`/<home>/...`) and clarify that prefix restoration logic properly handles both Unix root re-addition and Windows drive letter preservation. This ensures the `localhost` plugin documentation accurately reflects the actual implementation, improving the maintainability of the Tauri dependency tree.",
			"SHA": "a6f9fdd16342cbd3f82dd926abce63b7d37e76b5"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-03T08:10:37Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				173,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Deps): Format CHANGELOG.md with standard text wrapping\n\nReflow the introductory paragraphs and list items in Land/Dependency/CHANGELOG.md to conform to standard 72-character line wrapping and consistent paragraph spacing.\n\nThe changes are purely cosmetic, removing hard line breaks from narrative text while preserving the structured version history and commit references. This ensures the documentation is readable in standard terminal viewers and adheres to project formatting standards.",
			"SHA": "6f948ff7bf465c352b9c70d39f1556589c8dad05"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-03T00:32:48Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				173,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Deps): Update Tauri ecosystem submodules\n\nSynchronize all Tauri-related dependencies within the Land/Dependency/Tauri directory to their latest upstream revisions. This update advances the main Tauri submodule from 44be10b8 to 37f37fab, aligning core components (Studio, Forage) and essential plugins (ClipboardManager, WinRTNotification) with current upstream standards.\n\nAdditional tooling submodules including BenchMarkElectron, MeiliSearchDocsearch, TypeDocPluginMarkdown, VueCLIPluginTauri, and WryMobile are also updated. This ensures compatibility with the latest Rust/Tauri substrate and incorporates upstream bug fixes and stability improvements critical for the Land editor's native backend.",
			"SHA": "b76b5a373f74db9686b9d34306ab81b1e2e94c86"
		}
